{"ts":"2026-11-03T20:27:29.923Z","event":"hook","session":"111f5-a2e393ea0b48","seq":1,"tag":"fam","harness":"agy","decision":"allow","tool":"call_mcp_tool","server":"council_council","tool_call":{"args":{"Arguments":{"action":"discuss","round":"r2","text":"From the vantage of model-family diversity: models within the same family frequently share correlated blind spots, systematic priors, training distribution biases, and mutual sycophancy or failure modes. An independent reviewer from a *different* model family cuts right through intra-family blind spots, catching defects that same-family reviewers miss. For checking a plan like vsect maturation, a single cross-family independent reviewer captures the vast majority of the epistemic diversity dividend without incurring the coordination friction and token overhead of a full council. I lean towards recommending a single independent reviewer from another model family unless the plan contains high-consequence irreversible actions."},"ServerName":"council_council","ToolName":"council_submit"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"conversation":"3e2de62e-9a75-486b-bcd5-ef756ec06c2a","step":12,"model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low"}
