{"ts":"2026-11-03T20:27:49.306Z","event":"hook","session":"11304-a2e81741ddc8","seq":1,"tag":"fam","harness":"agy","decision":"allow","tool":"call_mcp_tool","server":"council_council","tool_call":{"args":{"Arguments":{"action":"speak","round":"r3","text":"I strongly support this motion. It aligns cleanly with the model-family diversity perspective: epistemic diversity is achieved primarily by breaking correlated failure modes across architectures/pre-training sets, which a single cross-family reviewer accomplishes directly. Crucially, condition 1 (verifier sees only the artifact and claims, not author reasoning) protects against cross-family sycophancy/priming, while condition 2 ensures falsifiable claim verification. Reserving councils for normative/trade-off decisions rather than raw verification is the exact right division of labor."},"ServerName":"council_council","ToolName":"council_submit"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"conversation":"3e2de62e-9a75-486b-bcd5-ef756ec06c2a","step":18,"model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low"}
