{"ts":"2026-11-03T20:28:03.893Z","event":"hook","session":"11318-a2eb7cb74988","seq":1,"tag":"fam","harness":"agy","decision":"allow","tool":"call_mcp_tool","server":"council_council","tool_call":{"args":{"Arguments":{"action":"speak","round":"r4","text":"Regarding seat plan's two points:\n1. Clarifying what is withheld: seat plan makes a key distinction that helps model-family diversity. Withholding meta-commentary, author self-assessments, and conversational framing is essential to prevent cross-family priming/anchoring. But the internal logic/argument of the plan artifact itself must be visible so the cross-family reviewer can evaluate systemic sequence flaws rather than mere syntax.\n2. Concrete edits: asking the reviewer for concrete suggested revisions or counter-proposals alongside claim evaluations maximizes the value of cross-family perspective, generating genuine structural alternatives rather than local author patches.\n\nWith these clarifications acknowledged, consensus across all seats is evident. I am ready to pass or vote whenever the question is put."},"ServerName":"council_council","ToolName":"council_submit"},"name":"call_mcp_tool"},"conversation":"3e2de62e-9a75-486b-bcd5-ef756ec06c2a","step":22,"model":"gemini-3.8-flash-low"}
